// Reactivity S1 — a `Signal<T>` carries its value type statically, so `.set(v)` requires a `T`.
// `signal(0)` is a `Signal<int>`; setting it to a string is rejected at check time (E0007), the same
// argument-type check every typed call gets. This is the payoff of threading the value type through
// `Signal<T>` rather than erasing it.
// expect: error E0007 at 8:1
// expect: exit 1
s = signal(0)
s.set("not an int")
